-- Digital Technology and Computer Applications course record. Safe to run more than once.
alter table public.courses add column if not exists video_url text;

insert into public.courses (slug, title, subject, credits, focus)
values ('digital-technology', 'Digital Technology and Computer Applications', 'Electives', 1.0, $j$Digital Technology and Computer Applications is a one credit elective that prepares students to use technology with skill, safety and integrity, and to serve God and others with it. Students study computer hardware and software, operating systems and files, digital citizenship and ethics, online safety and passwords, word processing and professional documents, presentation design, cloud collaboration, spreadsheets and formulas, charts and data analysis, how the internet and networks work, cybersecurity, research and evaluating sources, responsible use of artificial intelligence, algorithms and programming concepts, HTML and CSS, databases, digital media, technology careers and certifications, ministry technology, and building a digital portfolio. Every lesson is taught by Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr. with Scripture from the King James Version, and every unit includes a Focus, Topics, Assessments, Discussions and Quizzes, with a final digital portfolio and a final exam. The course is aligned at the strand level to Florida digital literacy and computer science standards.$j$)
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
